From 6a694e91df0c56e073c47d7ef7e1da4b8b64bbc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:48:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Support several nested initial grids per level in
 ReInitialize

NestedCosmologySimulationReInitialize walked the hierarchy by
descending the first-child chain, one grid number per level, so with
several nested grids on a level every patch was handed grid 0's IC
files, sibling patches' children were never visited, and the global
particle-count pass missed them too. Snapshot the whole hierarchy once
(recursing both links) and match each hierarchy grid to the initial
grid of the same level whose declared edges contain it, iterating
grid-number-major so particle-ID assignment stays deterministic and
the single-pyramid case reproduces the old ordering exactly. The
per-grid SubgridsAreStatic flag is now derived from the declared grid
list (any initial grid one level finer contained in this one). The
end-of-function reparenting pass and NestedRecursivelySetParticleCount
already handle arbitrary hierarchies and are unchanged.
---
 .../NestedCosmologySimulationInitialize.C     | 167 +++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 120 insertions(+), 47 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/enzo/NestedCosmologySimulationInitialize.C b/src/enzo/NestedCosmologySimulationInitialize.C
index d212fd6..8fce761 100644
